OL,3,GNEWSABenefits cheat who falsely claimed
OL,4,A#50,000 jailed
OL,5,
OL,6,FBy 2020 he said he was reliant on a
OL,7,Fwheelchair and was unable to work,
OL,8,Fhaving to pay a carer for help - but in
OL,9,F2023, he was seen leaving home in a
OL,10,Fvan, collecting colleagues and working
OL,11,Fduring the day.
OL,13,FAt Bradford Crown Court, he admitted
OL,14,Fdishonestly making a false
OL,15,Frepresentation to obtain benefits and
OL,16,Fwas jailed for 16 months.
OL,23,APub: 08-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
